M6 RESULT: both quantities measure demand overlap, but in different categories:
  p_c = Pr[S1=S2] is PROBABILISTIC (Renyi-2 collision mass), varies with theta;
  r_A = 1 is ALGEBRAIC (parity-fiber collapse), theta-independent.
Hence Fable ledgers are theta-affine, Kimi ledgers theta-free; no
gauge-respecting reparameterization can identify a nonconstant affine law
with a constant one.  This is the structural root of non-reducibility.
